node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.vercel/
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
*.log
reports/gsc-*.json
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Images are fetched at build time from lib/media.js, which records where each
# one came from and under what licence. The binaries themselves are not history.
public/img/destinations/
public/img/regions/
public/img/CREDITS.json
public/img/incoming/*
!public/img/incoming/.gitkeep
public/img/shared/

# Written by google-github-actions/auth (Workload Identity Federation). Holds no
# key, but it must never be committed by the import pull request.
gha-creds-*.json

# Preflight output of scripts/gsc-check.mjs. A log, never an input, never committed.
gsc-check.json

# Intermediate output of scripts/atlas/scale/generate.mjs. Twelve megabytes of
# pre-dedupe rows that dedupe-and-audit.mjs consumes and that generate.mjs
# reproduces in seconds. The deliverable is the deduplicated inventory beside it.
reports/scale-universe-*/_rows.jsonl.gz
reports/scale-universe-*/_raw-count.json
reports/livdar-master-seo-universe-*/_rows.json
__pycache__/

# atomic-write temporaries: these exist for milliseconds and must never be tracked
*.tmp
*.part

# NASA POWER shards are appended to while the fetch runs, which needs plain JSONL; the
# finalise pass gzips them and the .gz is what gets committed, like every other source.
data/atlas/sources/climate/power/*.jsonl

# GTFS pair aggregates are regenerable from scripts/atlas/ingest/gtfs-harvest.py against the
# Mobility Database catalogue, and the full set runs to hundreds of megabytes of stop graphs.
data/atlas/sources/transport/gtfs/
data/atlas/sources/transport/gtfs-national/

# LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.parquet crossed GitHub's hard 100 MB limit at 137 MB once
# the inventory reached 706,677 rows. It is a DERIVED artifact, regenerated by
# scripts/atlas/scale/run-1m-pipeline.sh, and LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.csv.gz carries
# the same rows in a portable form that is still tracked. Untracked rather than moved to
# LFS so the repository stays clonable without extra tooling.
reports/livdar-expiry-freeze-2026-09-30/LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.parquet

# The candidate roll-up partitions. data/atlas/candidates/ holds the SAME rows four times
# over, partitioned by family, by language, by market and by surface: 799,126 rows in the
# family partitions and 799,126 in the language partitions, verified identical. Only the
# family partition is tracked.
#
# This is not housekeeping. candidates/language=en/candidates.jsonl.gz reached 94 MB against
# GitHub's 100 MB hard blob limit, and the next manifest run would have pushed it over and
# hard-failed the push, which is exactly how LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.parquet had to be
# removed from this repository earlier. Untracking the roll-ups removes the cliff instead of
# waiting for it, and costs nothing: every one is regenerated by run-1m-pipeline.sh.
# WIDENED 2026-10-08 from the three roll-ups to the WHOLE partition tree, because the
# family partition crossed the limit too. When the roll-ups were untracked the largest
# remaining blob was 77 MB and I called that real headroom; the municipal pass added 89,353
# pages and took family=transport.city-pair-transit to 112 MB, and GitHub declined the push
# at the pre-receive hook. The headroom was not real, and the right fix is not to keep
# chasing it one partition at a time.
#
# Every file under data/atlas/candidates/ is a DERIVED EXPORT that run-1m-pipeline.sh
# regenerates from the manifest. The authoritative, auditable records stay tracked:
# LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.csv.gz, LIVDAR-1M-REJECTED-CANDIDATES.csv.gz, 1M-SUMMARY.json
# and the family, market and source breakdowns. Nothing that a count rests on is lost.
#
# _index.json is kept because it is small and says which partitions a run produced.
data/atlas/candidates/*/
!data/atlas/candidates/_index.json

# ---- the two authoritative CSV records are now carried as PARTS ------------------------------
# LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.csv.gz reached 97.4 MiB at 963,470 rows against GitHub's 100 MiB
# hard blob limit, and the target for this programme is 1,000,000 rows, which lands it at about
# 101 MiB. That cliff has already been hit twice here: LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.parquet had
# to be deleted, and family=transport.city-pair-transit was declined by the pre-receive hook at
# 112 MB - both times after I judged the headroom by eye and judged it wrong.
#
# These two files are NOT derived exports, so untracking them the way data/atlas/candidates/ was
# untracked would leave the repository without the evidence for its own number. Instead
# shard-manifest-for-git.py splits each on ROW boundaries into parts of about 30 MiB, three
# times under the limit. Every part carries the CSV header and is independently readable, and
# _parts-index.json records the row count and a sha256 over the concatenated data rows so a
# reader can prove the parts hold exactly the rows the monolith held, in order. Verified on
# 2026-10-08: 963,470 rows and 839,754 rows, headers identical in every part, sha256 match.
#
# The monoliths stay on disk and stay what every downstream stage reads locally.
reports/livdar-expiry-freeze-2026-09-30/LIVDAR-1M-CANDIDATE-MANIFEST.csv.gz
reports/livdar-expiry-freeze-2026-09-30/LIVDAR-1M-REJECTED-CANDIDATES.csv.gz
